mu reads and writes the notes of a Markupp server: text by default, the API payload with --json.

Usage:
  mu [command]

Examples:
  mu config set url https://markupp.example.com
  mu config show --json

Available Commands:
  completion    Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  config        Show and change the configuration
  graph         Read the graph, communities and links of a vault
  help          Help about any command
  invites       Answer the invites addressed to the account
  login         Log in to a server through the browser
  logout        Revoke the stored login and remove it from the config file
  members       Manage the members and invites of the tenant
  notes         List, read, write and search notes
  notifications List the notifications of the account
  status        Show the server, the login and the account; tokens are never shown
  tenants       List and create the tenants of the account
  tui           Browse and edit notes in an interactive interface
  vaults        Manage vaults, their members and their publication

Flags:
      --allow-plain-http   allow http:// outside localhost, sending the token unencrypted
  -h, --help               help for mu
      --json               print the API payload as JSON, unchanged
      --tenant string      tenant id, for accounts in several tenants (overrides MARKUPP_TENANT)
      --url string         server URL (overrides MARKUPP_URL and the config file)
  -v, --verbose            log each request as JSON on stderr
      --version            version for mu

Use "mu [command] --help" for more information about a command.
